Problem Description
This problem asks you to implement a Snake game with the following rules and requirements:

Game Setup:

The game is played on a screen with dimensions height x width
The snake starts at position (0, 0) (top-left corner) with length 1
Food items are provided as an array where food[i] = (ri, ci) represents the row and column position of the i-th food piece
Game Mechanics:

When the snake eats food, both its length and the game score increase by 1
Food appears one at a time - the next food item only appears after the current one is eaten
Food is guaranteed to never appear on a position occupied by the snake
Game Over Conditions:

The snake moves out of bounds (hits a wall)
The snake's head collides with its own body after moving
Implementation Requirements:

You need to implement a SnakeGame class with two methods:

SnakeGame(int width, int height, int[][] food): Constructor that initializes the game with the screen dimensions and food positions

int move(String direction): Processes one move in the given direction ("U" for up, "D" for down, "L" for left, "R" for right) and returns:

The current score if the move is valid
-1 if the game is over (snake hits wall or itself)





//In snake game, we have couple of things.
//we need to know the body of snake indices.

//the next move is within bounds.
//we need to move head forward, tail remove.

//if where head is moving -> if food is present or not.
//we can move to to tail and tail moved forward.




we can have dequue, for snake body.
and a hashset or unroderd set for collision check.



The key point is: food must be eaten in the given order.

In this problem, food is not "all food available on the board." It is a sequence of food positions.

Example:

food = {
    {1,2},
    {0,1},
    {2,3}
};

Initially:

foodIndex = 0

So the only food currently active is:

food[0] = {1,2}

Even if {0,1} is physically on the board, we don't consider it food yet.






Every move:

Calculate the new head position.
Decide whether the new head is on food.
If not eating, move the tail forward first.
Check whether the new head is now colliding with the remaining body.
Add the new head.
If eating, the tail doesn't move, so the snake grows.





class SnakeGame {
private:
    
   int wt, ht;

    vector<vector<int>> food;
    int foodIdx;

    // tail -> head
    deque<pair<int, int>> snake;

    // cell -> occupied
    unordered_set<int> occupied;

    int score;


public:

    SnakeGame(int width, int height, vector<vector<int>>& food) {
        foodIdx=0;
        wt= width;
        ht = height;
        score=0;

        snake.push_back({0,0});
        occupied.insert({0,0});
    }

   //store in the set an unique key of curr row and col.
    int getKey(int row, int col) {
       return row * width + col;
    }

    int move(string direction) {

         //head row, head col
         auto [hr,hc] = snake.front();

         //tail row,tail col
         auto [tr,tc] = snake.back(); 

        if (direction == "U") hr--;
        else if (direction == "D") hr++;
        else if (direction == "L") hc--;
        else if (direction == "R") hc++;

       //if it is a valid move
       if(hr<0 || hc<0 || hr>=wt || hc>=ht )
         return -1;

     //to put this in set., like viisted.
      int newKey = getKey(r, c);

      //check if new head has food, if new head has food, the snake size anyways grows so we wont remove tail.
      //also if we didnt eat , there is an edge case.
     // -> if i didnt eat, then we can move tail forward and occupy tail again.
     //if i did eat, then size will gorw and i can eat of tail.

      // Check whether we are eating food
        bool ate = false;

        if (foodIndex < food.size() &&
            food[foodIndex][0] == r &&
            food[foodIndex][1] == c) {

            ate = true;
            foodIndex++;
            score++;
        }

       if(!ate){
           //if i didnt eat
          //then remove tail

            snake.pop_back();
            occupied.erase(getKey(tr, tc));

          occupied.erase()
       }


       //now ate or not, we moved tail based on food was avaibale or not.

       Check collision with body
        if (occupied.count(newKey))
            return -1;


         // 7. Add new HEAD
        snake.push_front({r, c});
        occupied.insert(newKey);

        // 8. Return score
        return score;
        
    }
};







